{
  "info": {
    "name": "SCRUM-94 Roles and ownership",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "SCRUM-194/195/196 permission matrix (property-service).\n\nKeycloak setup: create case-sensitive REALM roles investor, realtor, lender and admin. Assign approved roles to users; do not assign professional/admin roles as realm defaults. Obtain a fresh access_token after changes. Only realm_access.roles from the validated JWT grants feature access. Client roles, persona, request bodies and organization IDs cannot grant a feature role. Every authenticated identity has baseline user access without needing an explicit user role. Users may hold multiple roles.\n\nBASELINE (any valid bearer token): property/search/details, valuation/history/forecast routes when present, comparables, property comparison, addresses/locations/parcels/map, image reads, prediction reads, read-only school/transport bulk lookups, favorites, profile/preferences, realtor license submission/status, saved searches, alerts/evaluation, contact requests, recommendations, user dashboard, mortgage and affordability calculations.\nINVESTOR or ADMIN: portfolios/holdings/financial records/summaries, scenarios, investor dashboard, opportunities/property opportunity score and investment calculations.\nREALTOR or ADMIN: clients/leads/tasks/transactions/CRM activities and realtor dashboard.\nLENDER or ADMIN: lender organizations/applications/imports/collateral and lender dashboard.\nADMIN only: all /api/admin/** and /api/ingestion/** routes, image imports/backfills (including job reads), prediction bulk writes, school/transport calculate-all and calculate-property-score writes.\nPUBLIC: Swagger UI/API descriptions and health/liveness/readiness. Other actuator paths and unclassified routes are denied. Existing configured CORS origins can preflight before authentication.\n\nScope: every personal resource remains owner-scoped, including for admins. A lender role does not imply organization membership. Lender application IDs must match the requested member organization. Only an organization owner manages membership. Foreign/missing private resources return 404; role denials return 403; missing/invalid JWTs return 401. Record IDs, owner fields and membership IDs are not feature grants.\n\nSubscriptions: NOT_CONFIGURED. There is no implemented billing/subscription approval contract, so no plan is inferred from persona or arbitrary JWT claims. License submission and selection of REALTOR persona do not grant the realtor role. Existing contact-directory categories do not certify credentials.\n\nManual setup: run against a test database. Use access_token for the current tester; switch it between an ordinary user, each professional role and admin. To test private ownership, create resources as account A using the existing feature collections, then read them as a second account B WITH THE SAME FEATURE ROLE. Fill foreign_* variables with A's IDs; never use a missing ID as the only ownership test. Foreign lender organization and mismatched application/organization are separate checks. No test in this collection deletes or changes business data.\n\nWorkflow checks: as an ordinary account PATCH /api/users/me with persona=REALTOR, then GET entitlements; realtorCrm must remain false and GET /api/clients must remain 403. Use the existing collections to verify foreign PATCH/DELETE attempts also return 404 without changing A's records. A lender organization member attempting membership changes must get 403; the organization owner succeeds. Repeat foreign-resource checks as an admin to ensure no ownership bypass. Existing access tokens retain their grants until replaced/expired; these endpoints do not administer Keycloak roles.\n"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
